# TG-03 network smoke (make smoke-tgd-net): tgd inside Zoraya under HVF with the Internet
# (run-qemu --net --net-open), started by the exact line of the report (tgd --grant, the
# test DC). No account and no secret: a placeholder api id (1) and a public test number,
# so Telegram's test DC answers API_ID_INVALID, which is the proof of a round trip through
# the grant. Then the memory (top, tgd stopped by Ctrl-Z), fg and a quit.
! panicked
! first process ended
! Traceback
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n~>
> mkdir tg\r
< \r\n~>
> grants @GRANT@\r
< \r\n~>
# A room to count tgd's memory in (top counts rooms; the session's row says 0K).
> room new tgdroom --mem 640M +w ~/tg\r
< \r\n~>
> room tgdroom\r
< \r\ntgdroom
# From ~: TDLib takes the realpath of the database directory, which needs ~ readable.
> cd ~\r
< \r\ntgdroom
> top\r
< \r\ntgdroom
> @GRANT@ --json\r
< "ev": "hello"
< "state": "need_credentials"
> {"op": "auth.credentials", "id": 1, "api_id": 1, "api_hash": "00000000000000000000000000000000"}\r
< "re": 1, "ok": true
< "state": "wait_phone"
> {"op": "auth.phone", "id": 2, "value": "9996621234"}\r
< "re": 2, "ok": true
< "message": "API_ID_INVALID"
> {"op": "status", "id": 3}\r
< "re": 3, "ok": true
# The memory with tgd connected and waiting for the phone: stopped (Ctrl-Z), top, fg.
> \x1a
< stopped
< \r\ntgdroom
> top\r
< \r\ntgdroom
> fg\r
~ 2000 @@no such text@@
> {"op": "quit", "id": 4}\r
< "ev": "bye"
< \r\ntgdroom
> status\r
< succeeded (exit status 0)
< \r\ntgdroom
x power off
> poweroff\r
